        "title": {
          "fr": "Un plan complet de l'Automation Framework",
          "en": "A complete Automation Framework plan"
        },
        "file": "zap.yaml",
        "lang": "yaml",
        "kind": "secure",
        "code": "env:\n  contexts:\n    - name: juice-shop\n      urls:\n        - http://juice-shop:3000\n      includePaths:\n        - \"http://juice-shop:3000.*\"\n      excludePaths:\n        # Never let the scanner log itself out\n        - \".*logout.*\"\n      authentication:\n        # The login is a JSON POST: ZAP replays it whenever the session is lost\n        method: json\n        parameters:\n          loginPageUrl: http://juice-shop:3000/#/login\n          loginRequestUrl: http://juice-shop:3000/rest/user/login\n          loginRequestBody: '{\"email\":\"{%username%}\",\"password\":\"{%password%}\"}'\n        verification:\n          # Poll an endpoint that only returns the e-mail when logged in\n          method: poll\n          pollUrl: http://juice-shop:3000/rest/user/whoami\n          pollFrequency: 60\n          pollUnits: seconds\n          loggedInRegex: '\"email\":'\n      sessionManagement:\n        # Reuse the token found in the JSON login response on every request\n        method: headers\n        parameters:\n          Authorization: \"Bearer {%json:authentication.token%}\"\n          Cookie: \"token={%json:authentication.token%}\"\n      users:\n        - name: scanner\n          credentials:\n            # Read from environment variables: no secret in Git\n            username: \"${ZAP_USER}\"\n            password: \"${ZAP_PASSWORD}\"\n  parameters:\n    failOnError: true\n    failOnWarning: false\n    progressToStdout: true\n\njobs:\n  - type: passiveScan-config\n    parameters:\n      maxAlertsPerRule: 10\n      scanOnlyInScope: true\n\n  - type: spider\n    parameters:\n      context: juice-shop\n      user: scanner\n      maxDuration: 2\n\n  - type: spiderAjax\n    parameters:\n      context: juice-shop\n      user: scanner\n      maxDuration: 3\n\n  - type: passiveScan-wait\n    parameters:\n      maxDuration: 5\n\n  - type: activeScan\n    parameters:\n      context: juice-shop\n      user: scanner\n      # Hard limits: a scan that never ends is a scan nobody runs\n      maxRuleDurationInMins: 3\n      maxScanDurationInMins: 20\n    policyDefinition:\n      defaultStrength: medium\n      defaultThreshold: medium\n      rules:\n        - id: 40018\n          name: SQL Injection\n          strength: high\n          threshold: low\n\n  - type: report\n    parameters:\n      template: traditional-html\n      reportDir: /zap/wrk\n      reportFile: zap-report.html\n      reportTitle: DAST report - Juice Shop lab\n\n  - type: report\n    parameters:\n      template: traditional-json\n      reportDir: /zap/wrk\n      reportFile: zap-report.json\n\n  - type: report\n    parameters:\n      template: sarif-json\n      reportDir: /zap/wrk\n      reportFile: zap-report.sarif.json\n\n  - type: exitStatus\n    parameters:\n      # Exit code 1 from a High alert, 2 from a Medium one\n      errorLevel: High\n      warnLevel: Medium\n",
        "note": {
          "fr": "`env` décrit **qui** scanner et **comment se connecter** ; `jobs` décrit **quoi faire**, dans l'ordre. Les durées maximales bornent chaque étape, la politique renforce la règle d'injection SQL, trois rapports sont produits et `exitStatus` transforme le risque le plus élevé en code de retour.",
          "en": "`env` describes **what** to scan and **how to log in**; `jobs` describes **what to do**, in order. The maximum durations bound every step, the policy strengthens the SQL injection rule, three reports are produced and `exitStatus` turns the highest risk into an exit code."
        }
